thod":"tex-environment-body-comments-removed","current_statement_sha256":"sha256:1dcc4b3c842f3a65266b04a2e00bb4c04eb76f9b0761556ecdcc5bbe997524f1","file":"preprints/A-counterexample-to-integer-degree-harmonic-dimension-comparison-September-25-2026/build/sections/introduction.tex","line":23,"producer_hash_method":"atlas-whitespace-normalized-text","producer_statement_sha256":"bdf1a325b2b3326ba8304f50de47f6a1be2283fab7773f0a9b8fe0cf2c9c00aa","provenance":{"kind":"computed","pin":"fd4aeeb2ee4fc729c18d98444fed42fd0529eeeb","source":"preprints/A-counterexample-to-integer-degree-harmonic-dimension-comparison-September-25-2026/build/sections/introduction.tex"},"sha256":"sha256:1dcc4b3c842f3a65266b04a2e00bb4c04eb76f9b0761556ecdcc5bbe997524f1","url":"https://github.com/openai/math/blob/fd4aeeb2ee4fc729c18d98444fed42fd0529eeeb/preprints/A-counterexample-to-integer-degree-harmonic-dimension-comparison-September-25-2026/build/sections/introduction.tex#L23"},"statement_kind":"theorem","text":"\\label{thm:main}\nThere are an even integer $n\\geq8$, an integer $k\\geq2$, and a complete\nsmooth metric $g$ on $\\mathbb R^n$ such that $\\operatorname{Ric}_g\\geq0$\nand\n\\[\n h_k(\\mathbb R^n,g)>h_k(\\mathbb R^n,g_{\\mathrm E}).\n\\]\nThe metric is Euclidean near the origin, and its asymptotic volume ratio\nsatisfies\n\\[\n 0<\\lim_{R\\to\\infty}\n \\frac{\\operatorname{vol}_g B_g(0,R)}{\\omega_nR^n}<1,\n\\]\nwhere $\\omega_n$ is the volume of the Euclidean unit ball."}
